\description{
Combines two ArcGIS layer packages from the Klamath Reservoir Reach Restoration
Prioritization (K3RP) fish screening project into one table: diversions downstream of Keno Dam
(\code{K3RP_FinalScreening_DSofKENO}, on the Klamath River and its tributaries) and diversions
upstream of Keno Dam (\code{K3RP_FinalScreening_USofKENO}, in the Lake Ewauna reach of the
Klamath River). Diversions were evaluated for fish-screening prioritization if they fell within
400 ft of expected anadromous fish distribution. Each diversion was scored on the size of the
diversion relative to its stream, the number of fish species (anadromous and resident native)
affected, and for the downstream reach only a fish-impact rating from ODFW fish biologists;
these roll up into a total score. The upstream-of-Keno layer has no stream name field of its
own, so \code{stream} is set to \code{"Klamath River"} for all of those rows, per the source
report.
